1
00:00:00,126 --> 00:00:03,129
I thought she had completely
erased me from her life.

2
00:00:03,212 --> 00:00:05,464
I resented her for so long, Enzo.

3
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:07,591
You're cute, huh?

4
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:09,093
You even understand my craziness.

5
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:12,430
It's like you always know
what to say when I get dramatic.

6
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:14,432
But seriously. You want to give it a try?

7
00:00:14,765 --> 00:00:15,558
Yes?

8
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,893
-It's for our Entrepreneurship Week.
-Ah.

9
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:20,354
I wanted to invite you there.

10
00:00:20,438 --> 00:00:22,815
Those bastards!
They're intimidating me again.

11
00:00:22,898 --> 00:00:24,984
-I'll call the police then.
-No, no. I have to go.

12
00:00:25,276 --> 00:00:27,820
-I have to go to Patricia.
-Relax. She will come, okay?

13
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:31,073
Miss D said she's on her way.
We still have 30 minutes left.

14
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:34,618
-Patricia!
-Mama.

15
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:36,454
You came.

16
00:00:50,926 --> 00:00:52,136
Good morning.

17
00:00:53,095 --> 00:00:54,513
Diana.

18
00:00:54,597 --> 00:00:56,932
-Ricardo.
-I've been waiting.

19
00:00:57,016 --> 00:00:58,726
-Uh, I'm sorry.
-Mama?

20
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:01,520
Flowers for you.

21
00:01:03,814 --> 00:01:05,357
-Thank you.
-This bouquet is a token

22
00:01:05,441 --> 00:01:06,942
of appreciation from our school.

23
00:01:07,026 --> 00:01:08,611
Please send my thanks, dear.

24
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:11,822
You made me worry.

25
00:01:12,156 --> 00:01:13,449
I wish you had waited for me.

26
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:14,867
I could have given you a ride.

27
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,327
Oh, I'm sorry, Ricardo.

28
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,620
But it would've been too late.

29
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:19,038
I was in a hurry.

30
00:01:19,622 --> 00:01:20,748
I'm sorry.

31
00:01:21,624 --> 00:01:23,083
Uh, Patricia, please don't get me wrong.

32
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:24,126
Uh…

33
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:27,379
All I care about is your mom's safety.

34
00:01:27,463 --> 00:01:30,591
We still don't know
who's behind those threats.

35
00:01:31,592 --> 00:01:32,843
What's going on?

36
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:36,347
Nothing. Ricardo and I just have
something to talk about.

37
00:01:37,181 --> 00:01:38,307
See you later, okay?

38
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:46,357
Mama's still receiving threats.

39
00:01:47,525 --> 00:01:49,026
She hasn't mentioned anything to me.

40
00:01:50,861 --> 00:01:53,072
I think she and Ricardo
are keeping it a secret.

41
00:01:55,658 --> 00:01:59,245
But… haven't they already decided
Sir Teddy is the suspect?

42
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,914
I talked to Uncle Teddy.

43
00:02:02,665 --> 00:02:05,459
I know he's not to be trusted.

44
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:07,753
But something tells me otherwise.

45
00:02:09,088 --> 00:02:11,298
What if he was telling the truth?

46
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:14,844
I'm trying to piece together how and where

47
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:16,679
it all started.

48
00:02:17,012 --> 00:02:17,847
You know…

49
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:19,515
everything had been going smoothly

50
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:21,809
since I started working here
in La Familia.

51
00:02:21,892 --> 00:02:23,853
There had been no critical concerns

52
00:02:23,936 --> 00:02:25,354
or major issues.

53
00:02:25,437 --> 00:02:28,482
It all began
with the food poisoning incident.

54
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:31,026
Oh. That caused her
a lot of stress, right?

55
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:32,611
It eventually led to her
having a heart attack.

56
00:02:32,695 --> 00:02:35,656
Mm-hmm. And Sir Ricardo's
blaming Sir Teddy for that.

57
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:37,867
A driver is testifying against him.

58
00:02:38,284 --> 00:02:40,411
Which Uncle Teddy denies.

59
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:43,873
Plus, there was not enough
evidence against him.

60
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,374
Soon after,

61
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:49,503
a video about the old fire went viral.

62
00:02:50,421 --> 00:02:51,922
It's as if they want to remind everyone

63
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,215
of what happened back then,

64
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:55,885
and of what Miss D has been concealing.

65
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:59,763
And so the media has been
more relentless against Miss D.

66
00:03:00,598 --> 00:03:03,058
Her leadership has become questionable.

67
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:06,770
But it's still not confirmed
who actually posted the video.

68
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:09,315
When the video about Grandma came out…

69
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:11,817
They wanted to make it seem
like Mama's not okay.

70
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:15,237
Basically, they want to bring Miss D down.

71
00:03:15,321 --> 00:03:18,532
To make everyone think:
Like mother, like daughter?

72
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:21,285
That Miss D was the one who
started the fire at the factory?

73
00:03:21,911 --> 00:03:24,538
You know, all of these things
are rooted in the past.

74
00:03:25,414 --> 00:03:27,333
Miss D is being haunted by the past.

75
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,085
The fire in La Familia.

76
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:32,838
That's what we need to uncover.

77
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:37,134
What exactly happened in the past?

78
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:48,020
They can't bury the hatchet!

79
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,563
Hey, watch out!

80
00:03:49,647 --> 00:03:51,649
You almost hit me!

81
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:55,152
I thought you were working
to keep them from reconciling.

82
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:57,321
That's why you've been getting
close to Patricia, right?

83
00:03:57,738 --> 00:04:00,240
So you can poison her mind against Diana,

84
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:03,619
and Diana will run to you when they fight.

85
00:04:03,953 --> 00:04:05,621
As long as I'm around,

86
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:08,165
they'll never settle their differences.

87
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,793
Diana isn't allowed to be happy.

88
00:05:28,203 --> 00:05:30,080
Is this how it's going to be?

89
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:39,631
You still don't understand why I did that.

90
00:05:41,008 --> 00:05:45,012
I just didn't want Diana
to think even less of you.

91
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:48,766
She already looks down on me.

92
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:50,559
And the only reason I took the money

93
00:05:50,809 --> 00:05:52,895
was because I knew you needed it.

94
00:05:53,312 --> 00:05:55,606
I had to swallow my pride.

95
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:58,817
That's why I didn't tell you and Patricia.

96
00:05:59,151 --> 00:06:01,987
Anything else you're hiding from me?

97
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:03,781
No.

98
00:06:04,907 --> 00:06:06,116
Nothing.

99
00:06:06,617 --> 00:06:09,661
That's why I feel so hurt.

100
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,622
You know…

101
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:15,125
No matter how hard things were,

102
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:18,212
we were happy as a family.

103
00:06:19,505 --> 00:06:22,674
But ever since Diana came back
into our lives,

104
00:06:22,758 --> 00:06:24,802
everything has fallen apart.

105
00:06:25,177 --> 00:06:27,554
Why do you let Diana affect you so much?

106
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:31,141
You don't understand how I feel!

107
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:32,976
It's like…

108
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:35,813
I was given something that…

109
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:37,815
could be taken away at any moment.

110
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:40,776
-I chose you.
-Did you really choose me?

111
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:43,362
Or did you end up with me

112
00:06:43,445 --> 00:06:45,739
only because Diana let you go?

113
00:06:45,823 --> 00:06:47,866
Carlota, we've been together
for a long time.

114
00:06:48,492 --> 00:06:49,993
We'll never fix this
if you keep thinking that way.

115
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:52,412
I'm here, with you.

116
00:06:52,663 --> 00:06:55,916
Please don't make me feel
like that's not enough.

117
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:57,626
Martin…

118
00:07:00,129 --> 00:07:03,006
I can't bear to lose you.

119
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:05,968
To lose you and our daughter.

120
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:08,804
Take away this fear from me.

121
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:14,810
Give me that one thing
you haven't given yet.

122
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:16,895
Maybe I'd be calmer when you do.

123
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:19,523
I love you so much.

124
00:07:30,409 --> 00:07:34,913
These are all inventory reports,
delivery receipts,

125
00:07:34,997 --> 00:07:37,124
and accounting records.

126
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:40,085
I also searched the internet,
but couldn't find anything.

127
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:45,966
It seems like all the news
about the fire is gone.

128
00:07:54,975 --> 00:07:56,226
Did you see something?

129
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:07,279
Mommy! Mommy!

130
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:13,994
Are you okay?

131
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:15,829
Hm.

132
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:17,706
Uh…

133
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:23,837
It's my mom.

134
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,505
You know…

135
00:08:26,215 --> 00:08:27,966
I often imagine…

136
00:08:29,635 --> 00:08:32,179
What if the fire never happened?

137
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:34,640
What if they're still alive?

138
00:08:37,935 --> 00:08:40,479
I'm sure I'll always treat them
to something.

139
00:08:41,021 --> 00:08:42,981
That's how they were with me back then.

140
00:08:47,236 --> 00:08:49,154
You know, I believe…

141
00:08:50,239 --> 00:08:53,367
They're very happy with where you are now.

142
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:57,412
They can see everything
you're doing for La Familia.

143
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,790
My loyalty to La Familia…

144
00:09:00,374 --> 00:09:02,251
My loyalty to Miss D…

145
00:09:02,584 --> 00:09:04,962
I do all that for them.

146
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:08,757
I just know they're very proud of you.

147
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:15,430
After all, you're not only
a great employee.

148
00:09:16,265 --> 00:09:18,976
You're also a very kind person, Enzo.

149
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:23,605
Thank you.

150
00:09:30,612 --> 00:09:31,655
Wait.

151
00:09:32,990 --> 00:09:34,491
I remember something.

152
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,912
When I was a kid…

153
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:43,000
Mommy always brought home
documents from the office.

154
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,751
If I'm right,

155
00:09:44,835 --> 00:09:47,921
there are documents
that weren't burned by the fire.

156
00:09:48,547 --> 00:09:50,924
And to this day, those documents
are still hidden.

157
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:21,621
Head of Corporate Communications,

158
00:10:21,705 --> 00:10:23,290
Nestor Manikan.

159
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:27,002
Nestor Manikan…

160
00:10:28,879 --> 00:10:30,047
Did you see anything?

161
00:10:32,716 --> 00:10:34,468
Nestor Manikan.

162
00:10:35,052 --> 00:10:36,803
His name sounds familiar.

163
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:02,204
I'm near Nestor Manikan's listed address.

164
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:03,705
I'll just ask around.

165
00:11:04,331 --> 00:11:06,958
I feel like he really knows
something about the fire.

166
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,086
Are you sure?

167
00:11:09,753 --> 00:11:11,963
Well, I have nothing to lose if I try.

168
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:14,674
Okay. Be careful.

169
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,344
I'm sorry I couldn't come with you.

170
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:20,138
Miss D has an important meeting
this morning.

171
00:11:20,222 --> 00:11:21,515
It's fine.

172
00:11:21,807 --> 00:11:24,559
I'll keep you updated, okay?
All right, bye.

173
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:27,646
Ma'am?

174
00:11:27,729 --> 00:11:28,855
Sorry. Excuse me.

175
00:11:28,939 --> 00:11:31,274
Do you know a Nestor Manikan?

176
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:35,112
Nestor? I don't know him, sorry.

177
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:36,446
All right, thank you.

178
00:11:38,031 --> 00:11:39,699
Uh, excuse me.

179
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:42,786
Why are you looking for my father?

180
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,125
My name is Patricia.

181
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:52,254
Are you Diana's daughter?

182
00:11:54,589 --> 00:11:56,633
I just wanted to ask something.

183
00:11:57,467 --> 00:12:00,011
Sure. What…

184
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:02,305
can I help you with?

185
00:12:03,056 --> 00:12:05,809
What do you know about the fire back then?

186
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:06,893
Nothing.

187
00:12:07,686 --> 00:12:08,687
I'm sorry.

188
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,273
I have no ill intentions.

189
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,485
I just want to know the truth.

190
00:12:15,569 --> 00:12:17,779
Miss D was very kind to our family.

191
00:12:18,447 --> 00:12:21,032
We owe Papa's life to her.

192
00:12:21,116 --> 00:12:23,618
She even paid for Papa's therapy!

193
00:12:32,377 --> 00:12:36,339
Ever since I was a child,
I have had a lot of questions.

194
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:39,342
Especially about my family.

195
00:12:39,426 --> 00:12:41,887
And I have never gotten
an answer until now.

196
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:46,933
Mister Nestor…

197
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:50,687
There is a reason you're given
a second chance at life.

198
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:54,608
Maybe it's time for you to tell the truth.

199
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:58,570
I don't want…

200
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:04,493
…to ruin someone's life.

201
00:13:07,913 --> 00:13:12,375
What if your silence has
already ruined someone's life?

202
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:17,631
Is that what happened to you, Patricia?

203
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:22,886
Was your life ruined?

204
00:13:26,264 --> 00:13:27,140
Why me?

205
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:30,810
What do you mean?

206
00:13:30,894 --> 00:13:37,150
I just followed Diana's orders.

207
00:13:38,193 --> 00:13:40,153
What I did was for you.

208
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:48,453
Oh, Patricia.

209
00:13:54,417 --> 00:13:56,878
-Go on in.
-Dear.

210
00:13:56,962 --> 00:13:58,964
-What are you doing here?
-I'll prepare some snacks.

211
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,385
What's wrong?

212
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,766
I spoke to your former employee,

213
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:12,269
Nestor Manikan.

214
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:15,897
What did you make him do?

215
00:14:15,981 --> 00:14:17,190
Nothing.

216
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:22,070
Why did you cover up
what happened in the fire?

217
00:14:24,656 --> 00:14:26,283
That's the only reason I can think of

218
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:28,118
why you don't want to revisit the past.

219
00:14:28,702 --> 00:14:30,370
-Patricia.
-What did you do?

220
00:14:32,956 --> 00:14:37,502
Did you really burn down La Familia?

221
00:14:38,587 --> 00:14:39,838
Don't you…

222
00:14:42,007 --> 00:14:44,342
Don't you remember
anything about the fire?

223
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:49,180
Did you light the candle at the factory?

224
00:14:49,264 --> 00:14:50,974
Patricia, tell me. What did you do?

225
00:14:56,396 --> 00:15:01,443
Are you still blaming me for it?

226
00:15:01,526 --> 00:15:02,736
No!

227
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:06,364
-I had nothing to do with it!
-Patricia!

228
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:09,534
I didn't burn down the factory!

229
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:11,578
Why did you have to lie?

230
00:15:11,995 --> 00:15:14,414
-Why?
-To protect you!

231
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:21,171
All the evidence
against Patricia has been erased.

232
00:15:21,254 --> 00:15:24,883
So it'll all point to Cecilia Pineda.

233
00:15:24,966 --> 00:15:26,676
Make sure nothing about this gets out.

234
00:15:29,596 --> 00:15:32,641
Do you understand why I had to do this?

235
00:15:32,724 --> 00:15:36,770
You don't have to explain it to me,
Ma'am Diana.

236
00:15:37,646 --> 00:15:38,813
I'm a parent, too.

237
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,858
I'm not a bad person.

238
00:15:42,317 --> 00:15:45,570
But I couldn't bear to see
my daughter's life ruined.

239
00:15:46,154 --> 00:15:48,323
You're the only one I can trust.

240
00:15:49,032 --> 00:15:52,869
No one can know that
Patricia was at the factory

241
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:54,663
when the fire happened.

242
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,668
To protect you!

243
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:02,504
To protect you!

244
00:16:05,423 --> 00:16:08,802
I knew they'd keep looking
for someone to blame

245
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:10,178
for what happened.

246
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:14,599
And because you're an Aragon,
you'd be the easiest target.

247
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:18,144
I knew they'd include you
in the investigation.

248
00:16:18,228 --> 00:16:22,315
And I couldn't risk them destroying you

249
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:24,442
just so they could close the case.

250
00:16:24,526 --> 00:16:26,403
It's clear to me now.

251
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,990
I didn't start the fire.

252
00:16:47,841 --> 00:16:48,967
I saw it myself.

253
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:54,389
The candle I lit wasn't
where the fire started!

254
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:58,017
And I believe you!

255
00:16:58,101 --> 00:17:01,312
You didn't do it!

256
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:04,107
None of this is your fault, dear.

257
00:17:19,873 --> 00:17:24,377
M-my whole life…

258
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:30,842
I thought you blamed me
for Grandpa's death.

259
00:17:31,426 --> 00:17:34,095
Oh, my god. No, dear. No.

260
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:36,306
Dear, no.

261
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:38,433
-No, no!
-Diana?

262
00:17:39,726 --> 00:17:41,102
Patricia?

263
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:45,356
What's going on here?

264
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:50,069
Patricia and I were just talking.

265
00:17:52,947 --> 00:17:54,616
Could you please leave us alone for now?

266
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:55,867
No.

267
00:17:59,954 --> 00:18:02,332
Patricia, are you fighting
with your mother again?

268
00:18:04,292 --> 00:18:06,085
What do you think she did this time?

269
00:18:07,712 --> 00:18:09,464
Patricia, Diana's doing everything she can

270
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:10,590
to get closer to you.

271
00:18:13,343 --> 00:18:14,636
You probably don't see it

272
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:15,929
because she just has
a different way of showing it.

273
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:18,139
You think she's cruel.

274
00:18:18,223 --> 00:18:19,724
You think she doesn't care about you.

275
00:18:21,643 --> 00:18:23,561
But your mother loves you
more than anything.

276
00:18:24,187 --> 00:18:25,396
Ricardo…

277
00:18:26,439 --> 00:18:30,944
Dear, let's talk another day, okay?

278
00:18:32,779 --> 00:18:33,738
Dear…

279
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:48,461
Let's go.

280
00:19:28,626 --> 00:19:30,253
Why did you bring me here?

281
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:32,672
Because you need it.

282
00:19:44,392 --> 00:19:47,478
-I think this is a bad idea.
-Diana…

283
00:19:47,562 --> 00:19:50,064
I just left Patricia like that.

284
00:19:50,982 --> 00:19:52,609
You both need to take a breath.

285
00:19:54,819 --> 00:19:56,070
What happened?

286
00:20:00,491 --> 00:20:02,076
I don't want to talk about it.

287
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:31,689
I don't know if I should be here.

288
00:20:31,773 --> 00:20:32,774
Diana.

289
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:45,787
I don't have to know what you
and Patricia talked about.

290
00:20:46,329 --> 00:20:48,122
I just want to help you clear your head

291
00:20:48,790 --> 00:20:50,583
and make your problems go away.

292
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:54,003
Just let it out.

293
00:21:04,389 --> 00:21:05,431
It's okay.

294
00:21:13,398 --> 00:21:14,899
I won't leave you, Diana.

295
00:21:16,859 --> 00:21:18,069
No matter what happens.

296
00:21:20,697 --> 00:21:22,240
Everyone else might leave,

297
00:21:23,366 --> 00:21:24,951
but I'll always stay by your side.

298
00:22:47,617 --> 00:22:48,993
Ricardo…

299
00:22:56,459 --> 00:22:57,460
What's wrong?

300
00:22:59,879 --> 00:23:02,215
We shouldn't have done it.

301
00:23:02,298 --> 00:23:04,383
Diana, come on.

302
00:23:05,802 --> 00:23:06,969
Even just for a day…

303
00:23:07,887 --> 00:23:09,388
I just want to be happy with you.

304
00:23:10,223 --> 00:23:12,475
-I'm sorry.
-It's okay.

305
00:23:13,184 --> 00:23:15,686
I'm just built this way.

306
00:23:15,770 --> 00:23:17,146
Whatever you are…

307
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:20,858
my feelings for you won't change.

308
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:25,530
-Can I ask you a favor?
-Sure.

309
00:23:26,114 --> 00:23:28,533
I hope you understand, but…

310
00:23:29,492 --> 00:23:33,538
I hope that no one knows about this.

311
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:36,082
I don't want to complicate things.

312
00:23:37,917 --> 00:23:39,210
I understand.

313
00:23:40,461 --> 00:23:41,671
I mean…

314
00:23:43,005 --> 00:23:44,173
you're the boss.

315
00:24:03,359 --> 00:24:05,403
What happened to your back?

316
00:24:08,281 --> 00:24:09,198
It was my father.

317
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:13,619
-I'm so sorry. I'm sorry.
-It's okay.

318
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:19,167
I'm sorry.

319
00:24:28,634 --> 00:24:30,303
-Thank you, Clara.
-Okay, ma'am.

320
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:47,486
Here are…

321
00:24:50,865 --> 00:24:52,200
the memos that need your signature.

322
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:11,594
About what happened…

323
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:14,680
All my life…

324
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:20,603
I've carried this heavy burden.

325
00:25:23,064 --> 00:25:25,399
I thought…

326
00:25:26,567 --> 00:25:29,946
you blamed me for the fire.

327
00:25:32,156 --> 00:25:33,908
I thought…

328
00:25:35,076 --> 00:25:37,119
you blamed me

329
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:41,332
for all the bad things
that happened to our family.

330
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:42,708
No, Patricia.

331
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:46,921
I'm sorry if that's what I made you feel.

332
00:25:47,588 --> 00:25:48,714
I was just…

333
00:25:48,798 --> 00:25:50,925
I was grieving back then.

334
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:53,844
I couldn't process my emotions properly.

335
00:25:54,929 --> 00:25:57,265
I'm sorry, dear. I'm sorry.

336
00:25:57,348 --> 00:26:00,226
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

337
00:26:02,853 --> 00:26:04,689
I'm sorry…

338
00:26:05,064 --> 00:26:07,149
I'm sorry, Mama.

339
00:26:16,158 --> 00:26:17,785
But you know,

340
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,954
even though the investigation was closed,

341
00:26:20,037 --> 00:26:22,581
it still haunts me.

342
00:26:23,165 --> 00:26:26,711
The past continues to haunt me.

343
00:26:27,545 --> 00:26:30,214
Why should you be the one to pay for it?

344
00:26:30,965 --> 00:26:33,342
You should've just let
the investigation continue.

345
00:26:33,426 --> 00:26:35,594
Then we would've found out the truth.

346
00:26:37,138 --> 00:26:38,306
Patricia…

347
00:26:39,849 --> 00:26:42,018
I'll take anything they throw at me…

348
00:26:43,144 --> 00:26:45,855
as long as your life doesn't get ruined.

349
00:26:52,069 --> 00:26:55,865
Mama… I'm not going to stop trying
to find out the truth.

350
00:26:58,367 --> 00:27:00,536
We can still make things right.

351
00:27:01,704 --> 00:27:04,999
Especially now that your life
is in danger.

352
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:08,711
You're being threatened
because they're blaming you.

353
00:27:09,253 --> 00:27:13,716
Patricia, let the police
do their job. Okay?

354
00:27:15,885 --> 00:27:20,765
Ricardo is already helping us
find whoever's threatening me.

355
00:27:21,515 --> 00:27:22,641
That's right.

356
00:27:22,725 --> 00:27:25,269
We need to find out who's behind it.

357
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:27,772
Could it be someone seeking revenge

358
00:27:28,189 --> 00:27:29,982
for what happened in the fire?

359
00:27:32,985 --> 00:27:36,447
What about… Cecilia?

360
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:40,117
Could she have something to do with this?

361
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:43,371
Don't you want to know the truth?

362
00:27:44,622 --> 00:27:47,500
Patricia, please stop.

363
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:50,252
Let me handle this.

364
00:27:51,921 --> 00:27:53,923
I won't let you get hurt.

365
00:28:03,933 --> 00:28:05,476
It can't be Cecilia.

366
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:06,811
She's dead.

367
00:28:08,270 --> 00:28:10,481
Do you think she really started the fire?

368
00:28:10,815 --> 00:28:12,233
That's what the investigation concluded.

369
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:13,984
What if it wasn't her?

370
00:28:15,194 --> 00:28:16,987
Maybe your lead is wrong, Patricia.

371
00:28:18,614 --> 00:28:22,618
If Cecilia wasn't the one
who started the fire at La Familia,

372
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:24,537
it could only mean one thing.

373
00:28:24,912 --> 00:28:28,165
It means my parents
still haven't gotten justice.

374
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,555
I had Ricardo investigated.

375
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:45,307
I'm sorry.

376
00:28:45,891 --> 00:28:48,477
But as I've said, if you have
an issue with Sir Ricardo,

377
00:28:48,561 --> 00:28:50,187
don't drag me into it.

378
00:28:51,605 --> 00:28:54,567
He said he has a child,
with no record to prove it.

379
00:28:54,984 --> 00:28:57,403
He said he's married,
but it was not registered.

380
00:28:57,778 --> 00:28:59,447
In all of his employment records,

381
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:01,907
he wrote his civil status as "Single."

382
00:29:02,616 --> 00:29:04,243
He told me he was never married.

383
00:29:04,326 --> 00:29:07,246
But there are no traces
of a family in his records.

384
00:29:07,329 --> 00:29:10,082
I also initiated
a digital footprint investigation.

385
00:29:10,166 --> 00:29:12,585
There's no existing evidence
of him having a family.

386
00:29:13,544 --> 00:29:16,589
No posts, no pictures, nothing.

387
00:29:18,174 --> 00:29:20,426
And all of his friends
and former co-workers,

388
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,761
they all said the same thing.

389
00:29:22,845 --> 00:29:23,971
They don't know anything.

390
00:29:24,555 --> 00:29:25,681
Is that possible?

391
00:29:26,182 --> 00:29:28,225
Aren't you just paranoid?

392
00:29:28,684 --> 00:29:29,894
You're a smart kid.

393
00:29:30,603 --> 00:29:31,687
Think about it.

394
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:33,564
La Familia's peace was disrupted

395
00:29:33,647 --> 00:29:35,441
when he entered the picture.

396
00:29:35,524 --> 00:29:39,195
Now, if you're really concerned
about your mother,

397
00:29:39,528 --> 00:29:41,447
think about what I'm saying…

398
00:29:43,115 --> 00:29:44,158
before it's too late.

399
00:30:08,098 --> 00:30:09,058
-Clara.
-Hm?

400
00:30:09,141 --> 00:30:11,060
-Is Miss D in her office?
-Not yet.

401
00:30:11,143 --> 00:30:12,311
She went out for a meeting.

402
00:30:12,645 --> 00:30:13,812
She hasn't come back yet?

403
00:30:13,896 --> 00:30:15,022
Not yet.

404
00:30:15,105 --> 00:30:16,690
-All right, thank you.
-I'll be over there.

405
00:30:19,610 --> 00:30:21,070
Hi. Yes.

406
00:30:21,153 --> 00:30:22,655
I'm sorry, I was in the elevator.

407
00:30:23,447 --> 00:30:25,324
Yes, I just got to the office.

408
00:30:26,534 --> 00:30:27,660
Diana…

409
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:30,913
You should sober up first
before coming in.

410
00:30:31,789 --> 00:30:34,208
Yes, don't worry. I won't tell anybody.

411
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:35,501
Okay, bye.

412
00:30:37,378 --> 00:30:38,546
Uh…

413
00:30:38,963 --> 00:30:40,506
Oh. Patricia.

414
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:42,466
What are you doing there?

415
00:30:42,883 --> 00:30:45,302
You were with Mama?

416
00:30:46,262 --> 00:30:48,681
And you had drinks? Is she drunk?

417
00:30:49,056 --> 00:30:50,266
Yes…

418
00:30:50,349 --> 00:30:52,017
We had a meeting outside the office.

419
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:56,564
The guest wanted us to drink
and we couldn't say no.

420
00:30:57,189 --> 00:30:59,775
I noticed you and Mama are getting closer.

421
00:31:00,734 --> 00:31:02,653
You're spending more time together.

422
00:31:03,028 --> 00:31:04,780
Other people have been noticing as well.

423
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:06,824
You two are always laughing together.

424
00:31:07,533 --> 00:31:09,326
Don't you want to see her laughing?

425
00:31:10,119 --> 00:31:12,413
I want my mother to be happy.

426
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:15,457
But I'm worried.

427
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:17,418
Because as the saying goes,

428
00:31:17,793 --> 00:31:19,795
"Too much laughter now

429
00:31:21,255 --> 00:31:23,841
might lead to so much sadness tomorrow."

430
00:31:28,429 --> 00:31:29,805
It's just a saying.

431
00:31:31,432 --> 00:31:33,726
Is there something going on
between you and Mama?

432
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:46,071
Patricia…

433
00:31:50,284 --> 00:31:51,660
I like Diana.

434
00:31:52,453 --> 00:31:54,705
I'm not married yet. I'm single.

435
00:31:55,706 --> 00:31:57,666
And your mother has been alone
for a long time.

436
00:31:58,500 --> 00:32:02,504
So I don't see anything wrong
with us liking each other.

437
00:32:03,672 --> 00:32:05,633
-Since when?
-Is there a problem with that?

438
00:32:08,010 --> 00:32:09,219
Patricia…

439
00:32:10,387 --> 00:32:12,890
You have nothing to worry about.

440
00:32:14,016 --> 00:32:17,227
Your mother is important to me.
I'm not going to hurt her.

441
00:32:17,978 --> 00:32:19,396
How about other people in your life?

442
00:32:20,731 --> 00:32:23,359
What exactly happened
between you and your ex-partner?

443
00:32:25,402 --> 00:32:29,073
I remember you told me
that you were never married,

444
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:31,325
but that doesn't mean you never loved her.

445
00:32:33,410 --> 00:32:35,037
Why did you break up?

446
00:32:38,415 --> 00:32:40,209
Let's just say that…

447
00:32:41,585 --> 00:32:43,921
we weren't compatible in a lot of things.

448
00:32:44,463 --> 00:32:46,799
We lived together for a few years,

449
00:32:47,383 --> 00:32:49,093
but ended up separating.

450
00:32:49,426 --> 00:32:50,928
Where is she now?

451
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:55,641
Don't you trust me?

452
00:32:56,767 --> 00:32:57,976
Ah…

453
00:32:58,060 --> 00:32:59,478
It's not that I don't trust you.

454
00:32:59,895 --> 00:33:03,691
I just want to make sure
my mom won't get hurt again.

455
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:05,943
Because you're right.

456
00:33:06,026 --> 00:33:07,903
My mother has been alone for a long time.

457
00:33:09,822 --> 00:33:11,198
But not anymore.

458
00:33:11,907 --> 00:33:13,784
She's no longer alone.

459
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,745
Because I'm back by her side.

460
00:33:38,726 --> 00:33:41,645
Gosh, you would never take no
for an answer, Ricardo.

461
00:33:41,729 --> 00:33:45,023
So, fine. I'll go with you.
You can stop nagging me.

462
00:33:45,107 --> 00:33:47,276
Where are you, anyway? I'm here.

463
00:33:47,860 --> 00:33:50,154
Okay, okay.

464
00:33:57,953 --> 00:34:00,914
Oh, Patricia. Why haven't you gone home?

465
00:34:00,998 --> 00:34:02,666
Want me to have Benjie drive you home?

466
00:34:03,167 --> 00:34:04,293
No need.

467
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:06,378
-Are you sure?
-Papa will fetch me.

468
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:08,088
Oh, okay.

469
00:34:09,256 --> 00:34:11,008
How about you? Are you going home?

470
00:34:11,091 --> 00:34:12,134
Not yet.

471
00:34:14,887 --> 00:34:17,347
You have plans with Sir Ricardo?

472
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:21,059
Yes. Patricia, is there…

473
00:34:21,643 --> 00:34:23,312
Is there something you want to ask me?

474
00:34:24,438 --> 00:34:26,648
Are you in a relationship
with Sir Ricardo?

475
00:34:26,732 --> 00:34:28,692
You see, I talked to him.

476
00:34:30,319 --> 00:34:32,196
He said he likes you.

477
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:35,199
We haven't gone public

478
00:34:35,783 --> 00:34:38,911
because I don't want anyone
putting meaning

479
00:34:38,994 --> 00:34:41,914
into our relationship
since we still work together.

480
00:34:42,581 --> 00:34:46,084
But, Patricia… I'm happy.

481
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:48,754
If that's the case, that's good.

482
00:34:50,214 --> 00:34:52,424
I just want you to be sure.

483
00:34:54,218 --> 00:34:57,554
How about you? How are you and Enzo?

484
00:34:58,555 --> 00:35:02,434
Are you happy? Are you sure about him?

485
00:35:10,943 --> 00:35:12,027
Patricia, dear!

486
00:35:12,528 --> 00:35:14,905
-Pa?
-Get in our car!

487
00:35:16,365 --> 00:35:18,200
Diana, see this?

488
00:35:19,201 --> 00:35:21,620
I've leveled up now. I've got a car.

489
00:35:21,703 --> 00:35:23,497
I can fetch Patricia now.

490
00:35:23,580 --> 00:35:26,250
She no longer needs to commute.

491
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:27,709
Good.

492
00:35:30,963 --> 00:35:32,089
I'll be off now.

493
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:56,697
Bye, dear.

494
00:35:59,867 --> 00:36:01,201
-Let's go?
-Yes.

495
00:36:08,542 --> 00:36:09,793
Let's go, Pa.

496
00:36:10,752 --> 00:36:12,129
Thank you.

497
00:36:26,935 --> 00:36:29,021
That Ricardo is such a show-off.

498
00:36:30,230 --> 00:36:32,024
Is he hitting on your mother?

499
00:36:32,900 --> 00:36:34,610
Wait, why are you asking?

500
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:37,362
Because he's so full of himself!
He thinks he's all that.

501
00:36:39,031 --> 00:36:40,073
Pa.

502
00:36:41,241 --> 00:36:42,826
If they do end up together…

503
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:47,873
…I don't see anything wrong about it.

504
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:51,877
Do you approve of Ricardo for your mother?

505
00:36:53,962 --> 00:36:56,256
As long as he doesn't hurt Mama.

506
00:36:58,050 --> 00:37:00,093
I'll just clean the car.

507
00:37:01,345 --> 00:37:03,597
Uh, P-Pa? By the way…

508
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:05,641
Um…

509
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:10,103
N-Nice car you got there.

510
00:37:11,438 --> 00:37:13,899
Looks like you love it so much.

511
00:37:13,982 --> 00:37:16,443
May I ask how you paid for it?

512
00:37:17,653 --> 00:37:19,488
Is it fully paid?

513
00:37:20,197 --> 00:37:22,616
Of course! It's fully paid!

514
00:37:23,325 --> 00:37:24,868
That's the fruit of my labor!

515
00:37:25,369 --> 00:37:28,747
And when my business grows,
I'll buy a brand-new one.

516
00:37:35,379 --> 00:37:36,880
You've been quiet.

517
00:37:36,964 --> 00:37:38,840
So, you told Patricia.

518
00:37:38,924 --> 00:37:42,511
I just told her that I have
good intentions for you

519
00:37:42,594 --> 00:37:43,887
so she wouldn't worry.

520
00:37:44,304 --> 00:37:45,639
What did she ask about?

521
00:37:45,722 --> 00:37:48,558
About my child and my ex-partner.

522
00:37:48,850 --> 00:37:50,143
What did you tell her?

523
00:37:50,227 --> 00:37:51,687
Diana, I think…

524
00:37:52,521 --> 00:37:55,232
you're the only one
who deserves an explanation

525
00:37:55,315 --> 00:37:56,483
because it's our relationship.

526
00:37:56,858 --> 00:37:58,068
Besides…

527
00:37:58,902 --> 00:38:00,445
it was just a one-night stand.

528
00:38:00,862 --> 00:38:03,532
Although we had a baby,
we were never together.

529
00:38:03,615 --> 00:38:05,492
Then, our child got sick.

530
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:08,453
You already know that, right?

531
00:38:08,537 --> 00:38:11,540
But we agreed to keep
our relationship to ourselves.

532
00:38:11,623 --> 00:38:13,709
Diana, are you ashamed of me?

533
00:38:15,043 --> 00:38:16,294
Of course not.

534
00:38:17,337 --> 00:38:20,048
But what if someone else finds out?

535
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:22,509
What if my critics
and detractors get wind of it?

536
00:38:22,592 --> 00:38:25,804
I don't want you to be their next target.

537
00:38:25,887 --> 00:38:29,266
Is that really the case,
or do you still have doubts about me?

538
00:38:30,559 --> 00:38:33,854
I understand why Patricia
is overprotective of you.

539
00:38:35,397 --> 00:38:37,024
But I'm not hiding anything.

540
00:38:37,983 --> 00:38:39,818
I hope you understand.

541
00:38:40,777 --> 00:38:42,779
Patricia and I are just starting
to get along.

542
00:38:42,863 --> 00:38:47,909
I just don't want anything
or anyone to get between us again.

543
00:38:47,993 --> 00:38:49,786
So, please…

544
00:38:49,870 --> 00:38:54,124
help me find the person
who wants to bring me down.

545
00:38:55,459 --> 00:38:57,169
So we can all be at peace.

546
00:38:58,503 --> 00:39:01,840
Actually, I heard something about Teddy.

547
00:39:03,216 --> 00:39:04,968
He's pestering Patricia.

548
00:39:05,052 --> 00:39:06,928
He's trying to poison
your daughter's mind.

549
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:10,932
I think he's targeting Patricia
because he can't get near you.

550
00:39:11,224 --> 00:39:12,934
Your brother has become desperate.

551
00:39:13,894 --> 00:39:16,646
He's grasping at straws.

552
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:19,316
But don't worry.

553
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:23,028
I'll handle him, okay?

554
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:38,126
That might be important.

555
00:39:41,296 --> 00:39:42,964
You're more important.

556
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:02,859
-Hi!
-Next time, just text me.

557
00:40:02,943 --> 00:40:05,654
Don't call unless it's an emergency.

558
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:07,697
Diana almost caught me earlier.

559
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:10,325
Well, I'm sorry, okay?

560
00:40:10,408 --> 00:40:12,911
You didn't call or text.

561
00:40:12,994 --> 00:40:14,788
-I got worried.
-Sandra.

562
00:40:15,038 --> 00:40:17,332
I can't afford to give them
any reason to doubt me.

563
00:40:17,791 --> 00:40:19,084
Patricia's starting to ask questions.

564
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,211
I assume you managed
to appease her curiosity.

565
00:40:21,294 --> 00:40:23,213
Yes, but she's still suspicious.

566
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:27,175
Too bad. She might just
be the one to thwart your plans.

567
00:40:28,301 --> 00:40:29,636
All good to go.

568
00:40:29,928 --> 00:40:31,054
Thank you.

569
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:37,185
Hm? I know that look.

570
00:40:37,894 --> 00:40:39,354
Is something bothering you?

571
00:40:39,896 --> 00:40:41,481
I get that you're concerned.

572
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:45,861
Dear…

573
00:40:46,987 --> 00:40:49,739
No matter what happens
between Ricardo and me,

574
00:40:49,823 --> 00:40:51,283
we will face it.

575
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:54,703
We've made this decision together.

576
00:40:55,579 --> 00:40:58,081
And wherever this leads…

577
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:00,959
we'll be responsible for ourselves.

578
00:41:06,673 --> 00:41:08,466
I get that.

579
00:41:09,676 --> 00:41:13,972
I just want you to be sure
about Sir Ricardo.

580
00:41:14,514 --> 00:41:16,641
Ricardo told me…

581
00:41:18,059 --> 00:41:20,353
that Teddy is pestering you.

582
00:41:20,437 --> 00:41:23,607
I think Uncle Teddy has a point.

583
00:41:24,232 --> 00:41:27,569
We still don't know everything
about Sir Ricardo.

584
00:41:27,652 --> 00:41:29,529
Especially about his personal life.

585
00:41:29,613 --> 00:41:32,490
Dear, he's a very private person.

586
00:41:33,867 --> 00:41:36,077
I know he had a child,

587
00:41:36,703 --> 00:41:39,831
but he never had a relationship
with the mother.

588
00:41:42,042 --> 00:41:43,168
Oh.

589
00:41:44,211 --> 00:41:45,670
-Hi.
-Hi.

590
00:41:46,379 --> 00:41:49,174
Let's go? We're running late
for our lunch meeting.

591
00:41:49,257 --> 00:41:50,342
Okay.

592
00:41:56,473 --> 00:41:58,808
I'll see you later, dear. We have to go.

593
00:41:59,684 --> 00:42:00,936
Hmm?

594
00:42:13,156 --> 00:42:15,075
Dad? Dad.

595
00:42:15,158 --> 00:42:16,993
Dad! Wake up, Dad!

596
00:42:17,077 --> 00:42:18,245
Dad!

597
00:42:19,329 --> 00:42:21,539
You haven't settled last month's
electricity bill.

598
00:42:21,623 --> 00:42:23,416
Now, we have a disconnection notice.

599
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,502
-Have you seen this?
-I'll handle it.

600
00:42:26,086 --> 00:42:29,422
Hey! I can't even talk to you properly!

601
00:42:29,506 --> 00:42:30,715
Have you seen yourself?

602
00:42:33,260 --> 00:42:35,387
See?! Dad, you're obsessed!

603
00:42:36,972 --> 00:42:42,769
-You're still on to Ricardo?
-I will exterminate that pest.

604
00:42:44,896 --> 00:42:48,692
I know he's the vermin
that's infesting La Familia.

605
00:42:53,947 --> 00:42:54,781
Hello?

606
00:42:56,700 --> 00:42:58,243
What did you find about Ricardo?

607
00:43:13,133 --> 00:43:16,011
Diana! Diana, please!

608
00:43:16,094 --> 00:43:18,430
-Teddy, what is it this time?
-Please, listen to me.

609
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:19,973
I found something about Ricardo.

610
00:43:21,016 --> 00:43:22,767
Teddy, will you stop it? My--

611
00:43:22,851 --> 00:43:25,020
Just take a look at it, please.
Someone took a photo of him

612
00:43:25,103 --> 00:43:26,438
with a Quick Bites staff.

613
00:43:26,855 --> 00:43:28,064
Please.

614
00:43:31,901 --> 00:43:33,194
That's proof.

615
00:43:33,445 --> 00:43:35,071
I'm not the spy.

616
00:43:35,822 --> 00:43:37,532
I'm not the one planning
La Familia's downfall.

617
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:38,867
It's Ricardo.

618
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:42,287
Think about it. The reporter,
the attack against you,

619
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:44,164
the poisoning, it wasn't me!

620
00:43:45,040 --> 00:43:46,624
Ricardo was the one behind all of it.

621
00:43:46,708 --> 00:43:49,711
Now, did you find
strong evidence against me? No.

622
00:43:49,794 --> 00:43:51,046
This is proof.

623
00:43:51,296 --> 00:43:53,590
Are you going to let yourself
be fooled by a man again?

624
00:43:57,260 --> 00:43:59,763
Send me the picture.
I'll have it investigated.

625
00:44:00,555 --> 00:44:01,806
Let's go, Benjie.

626
00:44:15,987 --> 00:44:17,197
Miss D?

627
00:44:17,447 --> 00:44:19,949
Have you asked an expert
about the photo yet?

628
00:44:20,867 --> 00:44:21,826
Yes, Miss D.

629
00:44:22,118 --> 00:44:24,496
They already checked
the file data and image details.

630
00:44:25,163 --> 00:44:28,041
They found no signs
that it was digitally altered

631
00:44:28,124 --> 00:44:29,334
or AI-generated.

632
00:44:29,876 --> 00:44:31,920
The image is authentic, Miss D.

633
00:44:32,003 --> 00:44:34,714
The thing I asked you to do…
Where's the driver?

634
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:37,509
As per our logistics manager,

635
00:44:37,967 --> 00:44:39,386
the driver went AWOL

636
00:44:39,469 --> 00:44:42,180
after he gave his testimony
against Sir Teddy.

637
00:44:42,597 --> 00:44:45,183
To this day, he still hasn't returned.

638
00:44:45,266 --> 00:44:46,726
They don't know where he went.

639
00:44:52,399 --> 00:44:54,317
Good thing we finished early.

640
00:44:54,943 --> 00:44:56,694
Hey, let me drop you off.

641
00:44:57,987 --> 00:44:59,989
Don't you think Sir Ricardo
has something to do

642
00:45:00,073 --> 00:45:01,449
with the threats against Miss D?

643
00:45:03,451 --> 00:45:05,578
Why would he do that?

644
00:45:07,455 --> 00:45:09,416
Where was he again when the fire happened?

645
00:45:10,625 --> 00:45:12,377
That was in 2008.

646
00:45:13,920 --> 00:45:16,131
Wait. It should be on his CV.

647
00:45:17,549 --> 00:45:18,800
Uh…

648
00:45:20,218 --> 00:45:23,263
It says here that he was working
at a PR firm in Indonesia

649
00:45:23,346 --> 00:45:24,556
during that time.

650
00:45:41,322 --> 00:45:42,657
We're not going home just yet.

651
00:45:42,949 --> 00:45:43,992
Huh?

652
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,317
Excuse me.

653
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:20,278
-Is the doctor in?
-Yes, sir. He's on his way.

654
00:46:20,361 --> 00:46:22,447
You're such a kind son, Sir Ricardo.

655
00:46:22,530 --> 00:46:24,491
Your mother is lucky
to have a son like you.

656
00:46:25,617 --> 00:46:27,452
-Thank you.
-I'll take you there, sir.

657
00:46:27,535 --> 00:46:28,453
Okay.

658
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:38,296
Enzo, did I hear that right?

659
00:46:38,379 --> 00:46:40,757
He's going to visit his mother?

660
00:46:41,758 --> 00:46:42,967
Uh…

661
00:46:45,345 --> 00:46:46,429
Let's follow him.

662
00:46:46,513 --> 00:46:48,014
Patricia, wait!

663
00:46:57,273 --> 00:46:58,483
I can't see clearly.

664
00:47:08,117 --> 00:47:10,703
Patricia, he'll see us!

665
00:47:21,297 --> 00:47:24,384
We followed Sir Ricardo
to the hospital, Miss D.

666
00:47:25,260 --> 00:47:27,595
He was looking after an elderly woman.

667
00:47:27,971 --> 00:47:30,765
Who was the old lady
he visited at the hospital?

668
00:47:31,057 --> 00:47:32,141
His mother.

669
00:47:33,017 --> 00:47:34,644
What? I--

670
00:47:34,727 --> 00:47:37,355
Enzo, remember?
I had you check his background.

671
00:47:37,438 --> 00:47:38,773
Exactly, Miss D.

672
00:47:38,982 --> 00:47:40,650
And that's what surprised me.

673
00:47:41,109 --> 00:47:43,278
Because based on the information
I gathered about him,

674
00:47:43,695 --> 00:47:46,197
both his parents were declared deceased.

675
00:47:49,742 --> 00:47:52,579
Why are you with
the executive of Quick Bites?

676
00:47:52,870 --> 00:47:54,914
I did my own investigation.

677
00:47:54,998 --> 00:47:57,584
I talked to this person to find out if…

678
00:47:57,959 --> 00:47:59,627
it's true that Teddy's
conspiring with them.

679
00:48:13,141 --> 00:48:15,018
That's one of the files
in Teddy's investigation.

680
00:48:16,311 --> 00:48:17,895
But I'm still verifying it.

681
00:48:19,689 --> 00:48:20,940
That's not all.

682
00:48:21,399 --> 00:48:25,320
Your personal details
on your resume don't add up.

683
00:48:25,695 --> 00:48:26,863
What are you talking about?

684
00:48:26,946 --> 00:48:30,033
It states there
that both your parents are dead.

685
00:48:30,366 --> 00:48:32,535
Who are you visiting at the hospital then?

686
00:48:32,619 --> 00:48:34,287
Are you having someone tail me?

687
00:48:34,579 --> 00:48:35,830
I need to know the truth.

688
00:48:36,706 --> 00:48:38,374
Those are personal details.

689
00:48:38,791 --> 00:48:40,460
I can't help but be suspicious.

690
00:48:43,171 --> 00:48:45,840
Lately, your actions have been suspicious.

691
00:48:46,132 --> 00:48:47,634
You're talking to someone on the phone

692
00:48:47,717 --> 00:48:49,636
but you won't say who.

693
00:48:49,927 --> 00:48:51,012
And now I found out…

694
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:53,931
you're still hiding something
about your life.

695
00:48:54,849 --> 00:48:56,643
When my mother died…

696
00:49:00,021 --> 00:49:01,606
someone took care of me.

697
00:49:03,816 --> 00:49:05,693
She treated me like her own son.

698
00:49:06,819 --> 00:49:08,696
So the information you got is correct.

699
00:49:12,408 --> 00:49:14,619
I visit my mother at the hospital.

700
00:49:15,703 --> 00:49:17,163
But not for long.

701
00:49:19,123 --> 00:49:20,917
Her time is running out.

702
00:49:23,252 --> 00:49:25,421
I didn't mention it to you because…

703
00:49:27,924 --> 00:49:30,760
I just want us to be happy
when we're together.

704
00:49:32,178 --> 00:49:33,638
Who told you this?

705
00:49:35,807 --> 00:49:36,974
Was it Teddy?

706
00:49:38,810 --> 00:49:40,228
Patricia?

707
00:49:42,146 --> 00:49:44,774
Diana, I understand you
because they're your family.

708
00:49:45,775 --> 00:49:47,360
So you should believe them.

709
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:51,864
Do you have any more questions?

710
00:49:54,701 --> 00:49:55,910
Okay.

711
00:50:05,628 --> 00:50:07,588
Was it wrong of me to ask?

712
00:50:07,672 --> 00:50:09,132
Was what I did wrong?

713
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:13,761
I just wanted to protect
the interests of the company.

714
00:50:13,845 --> 00:50:15,722
And I hoped that…

715
00:50:19,726 --> 00:50:23,146
my own brother didn't betray me.

716
00:50:23,980 --> 00:50:27,817
So you believed
Ricardo was the one scheming all this?

717
00:50:29,360 --> 00:50:31,988
Do I always have to choose
between two things?

718
00:50:34,824 --> 00:50:37,827
I know that Ricardo is upset with me.

719
00:50:38,286 --> 00:50:39,912
But I can't help but be suspicious.

720
00:50:40,413 --> 00:50:44,125
I've been betrayed many times
by the people around me.

721
00:50:44,834 --> 00:50:46,627
You're just scared.

722
00:50:47,920 --> 00:50:49,464
Is it wrong of me to be suspicious?

723
00:50:50,423 --> 00:50:52,675
You're scared of yourself.

724
00:50:53,509 --> 00:50:55,470
Of your own feelings.

725
00:50:57,221 --> 00:51:02,602
When you sense something wrong,
you dwell on it.

726
00:51:03,811 --> 00:51:09,317
You're scared of giving Ricardo a chance.

727
00:51:10,693 --> 00:51:13,112
You're scared of making mistakes again.

728
00:51:21,496 --> 00:51:23,414
Have you seen Ricardo?

729
00:51:23,664 --> 00:51:25,833
I don't think I've seen him today, Miss D.

730
00:51:28,169 --> 00:51:29,212
Oh.

731
00:51:32,006 --> 00:51:33,674
Diana, can we talk?

732
00:51:34,801 --> 00:51:35,968
Excuse me.

733
00:51:42,016 --> 00:51:43,810
My resignation letter.

734
00:51:50,983 --> 00:51:53,945
I know I still have
to render 30 more days.

735
00:51:54,028 --> 00:51:55,154
Correct?

736
00:51:56,823 --> 00:51:57,824
Why?

737
00:51:57,907 --> 00:52:00,493
Diana, I can't stay in a place…

738
00:52:02,578 --> 00:52:04,622
where no one trusts me.

739
00:52:10,169 --> 00:52:12,797
Well, if that's your decision,
there's nothing I can do.

740
00:52:14,257 --> 00:52:16,342
Just make sure that the turnover…

741
00:52:17,260 --> 00:52:19,470
to your replacement…

742
00:52:20,721 --> 00:52:22,390
goes smoothly.

743
00:52:31,774 --> 00:52:32,775
Hello?

744
00:52:34,902 --> 00:52:36,153
What?!

745
00:52:37,405 --> 00:52:39,532
Wh--Why? What happened?!

746
00:52:41,325 --> 00:52:42,368
Huh?!

747
00:52:42,451 --> 00:52:44,203
All right, nurse. I'll be on my way.

748
00:52:44,287 --> 00:52:46,622
Uh… Wh-What happened?

749
00:52:46,706 --> 00:52:47,957
I have to go.

750
00:52:49,458 --> 00:52:51,627
M-My mother needs me at the hospital.

751
00:52:53,045 --> 00:52:54,255
Enzo!

752
00:52:56,716 --> 00:52:57,842
Miss D? Everything okay?

753
00:52:57,925 --> 00:52:59,969
Where did you follow Ricardo?
What hospital?

754
00:53:00,261 --> 00:53:02,221
At St. Gabriel Hospital.

755
00:53:02,889 --> 00:53:04,682
Call Benjie.
Tell him to get the car ready.

756
00:53:04,765 --> 00:53:06,767
-Right now. Hurry!
-Okay, Miss D.

757
00:53:22,450 --> 00:53:23,659
Ricardo.

758
00:53:24,285 --> 00:53:25,912
Ricardo, I'm so sorry.

759
00:53:26,329 --> 00:53:27,622
I'm very sorry.

760
00:53:28,456 --> 00:53:29,957
What are you doing here?

761
00:53:30,374 --> 00:53:31,667
I was worried about you.

762
00:53:33,085 --> 00:53:34,420
What's her name?

763
00:53:37,506 --> 00:53:38,424
Mama Esther.

764
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:42,219
Is there anything I can--

765
00:53:43,179 --> 00:53:44,138
Anything I can do?

766
00:53:46,307 --> 00:53:47,642
-How can I help?
-Don't.

767
00:53:47,934 --> 00:53:49,185
There's no need, Diana.

768
00:53:50,186 --> 00:53:51,604
I can handle this myself.

769
00:53:53,731 --> 00:53:54,857
Go home.

770
00:54:15,127 --> 00:54:16,504
Where's Miss D?

771
00:54:16,587 --> 00:54:18,381
She was in a hurry to leave earlier.

772
00:54:18,464 --> 00:54:20,383
She went to see Sir Ricardo
at the hospital.

773
00:54:20,841 --> 00:54:21,801
Why? What happened?

774
00:54:22,134 --> 00:54:23,970
Sir Ricardo resigned.

775
00:54:24,053 --> 00:54:25,429
Maybe it's because of that.

776
00:54:25,763 --> 00:54:27,598
Sir Ricardo resigned?

777
00:54:32,728 --> 00:54:34,563
Oh, where are you going?

778
00:54:34,814 --> 00:54:35,982
To the hospital.

779
00:54:37,483 --> 00:54:38,609
Hey.

780
00:54:44,949 --> 00:54:48,285
Nurse, where's the patient who was here?

781
00:54:48,536 --> 00:54:49,870
What's your relationship to the patient?

782
00:54:50,329 --> 00:54:51,455
Um…

783
00:54:51,539 --> 00:54:55,084
I'm acquainted with her son,
Ricardo Salvador.

784
00:54:55,751 --> 00:54:57,169
How's the patient?

785
00:54:57,920 --> 00:54:59,422
She just passed away earlier.

786
00:55:01,048 --> 00:55:03,134
Oh… Is that so?

787
00:55:05,761 --> 00:55:07,263
Why are you also wearing black?

788
00:55:08,681 --> 00:55:11,851
Well, I guess we're the only ones
who can mourn her.

789
00:55:11,934 --> 00:55:14,854
She's pitiful, isn't she?
She doesn't have any family.

790
00:55:15,730 --> 00:55:16,856
Yes, right.

791
00:55:30,619 --> 00:55:31,996
Oh, yes, I am.

792
00:55:34,999 --> 00:55:37,793
Did they mention any plans for the wake?

793
00:55:38,085 --> 00:55:39,045
No.

794
00:55:39,587 --> 00:55:40,546
What do you mean, no?

795
00:55:40,629 --> 00:55:42,048
But I heard earlier

796
00:55:42,298 --> 00:55:43,841
that they will bring the ashes home

797
00:55:43,924 --> 00:55:45,468
after the cremation.

798
00:55:47,094 --> 00:55:49,138
-Thank you.
-Excuse me, ma'am.

799
00:55:58,939 --> 00:56:01,859
All my files
related to La Familia are in here.

800
00:56:02,568 --> 00:56:04,236
I'll leave them here for now.

801
00:56:06,072 --> 00:56:08,240
If that's not enough,

802
00:56:09,784 --> 00:56:10,868
just let me know.

803
00:56:11,827 --> 00:56:12,703
What's your plan now?

804
00:56:13,871 --> 00:56:14,914
I'll leave it to fate.

805
00:56:15,498 --> 00:56:18,709
I'm sure there's still a job
waiting for me in Indonesia.

806
00:56:19,168 --> 00:56:21,045
Don't take this the wrong way.

807
00:56:23,756 --> 00:56:26,759
I just want to know. How are you?

808
00:56:27,551 --> 00:56:29,845
I still care about you, Ricardo.

809
00:56:30,721 --> 00:56:31,889
I do, too.

810
00:56:32,723 --> 00:56:34,350
I still care for you.

811
00:56:34,934 --> 00:56:37,978
My feelings for you
will never go away, Diana.

812
00:56:38,938 --> 00:56:40,481
I just don't want to force it anymore.

813
00:56:41,440 --> 00:56:44,568
Maybe Patricia really doesn't
want me to be with you.

814
00:56:44,985 --> 00:56:47,905
That's why she still won't stop
investigating me.

815
00:56:50,658 --> 00:56:52,409
Maybe it's because…

816
00:56:52,827 --> 00:56:55,246
my explanations to you
still aren't enough.

817
00:56:55,329 --> 00:56:57,790
I didn't ask Patricia
to do anything like that.

818
00:57:00,084 --> 00:57:02,503
The person who died
was like a mother to him.

819
00:57:03,170 --> 00:57:04,755
Won't they hold at least a mass for her?

820
00:57:05,506 --> 00:57:06,924
Doesn't she have any relatives?

821
00:57:07,174 --> 00:57:09,176
Why does she have
to be cremated right away?

822
00:57:12,388 --> 00:57:13,806
Patricia.

823
00:57:13,889 --> 00:57:15,057
Ma.

824
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:20,896
Didn't I tell you to stop investigating?

825
00:57:21,355 --> 00:57:23,983
-But, Ma--
-Ricardo just lost someone.

826
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:25,860
He's grieving.

827
00:57:26,152 --> 00:57:28,571
Does he have to explain
everything he does?

828
00:57:29,697 --> 00:57:32,241
He's in a very difficult situation.

829
00:57:32,533 --> 00:57:36,203
Please stop asking him questions, okay?

830
00:57:37,788 --> 00:57:39,206
Am I understood?

831
00:57:43,210 --> 00:57:45,671
-Yes, Ma.
-Thank you.

832
00:57:56,390 --> 00:57:59,351
Just leave them on my table.
I'll just go see Ricardo.

833
00:57:59,435 --> 00:58:00,561
Okay, Miss D.

834
00:58:04,815 --> 00:58:06,442
Yes, I'm just taking care of something.

835
00:58:06,692 --> 00:58:08,110
But I'm on my way.

836
00:58:08,527 --> 00:58:09,987
Same restaurant?

837
00:58:11,363 --> 00:58:12,823
Okay, I can't stay long, okay?

838
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:15,743
Okay.

839
00:58:26,921 --> 00:58:28,964
Benjie, get the car ready.
I'm coming down.

840
00:58:35,846 --> 00:58:37,681
Reservation for Sandra?

841
00:58:38,265 --> 00:58:40,351
-This way, sir.
-Thank you.

842
00:58:49,485 --> 00:58:50,986
-Hi.
-Hi.

843
00:58:54,448 --> 00:58:55,407
Did you fix it already?

844
00:58:55,491 --> 00:58:56,533
Mh-mm.

845
00:59:11,215 --> 00:59:12,341
Ricardo.

846
00:59:15,970 --> 00:59:17,054
Diana.

847
00:59:26,480 --> 00:59:28,148
Ricardo was the one behind all of it!

848
00:59:28,232 --> 00:59:29,358
Teddy, will you stop it?

849
00:59:29,441 --> 00:59:32,069
The way he kicked Uncle Teddy out…

850
00:59:32,152 --> 00:59:33,988
It's like he's having fun with it.

851
00:59:34,071 --> 00:59:36,073
-It's Sir Ricardo.
-What about him?

852
00:59:36,156 --> 00:59:37,408
He's like a different person.

853
00:59:37,491 --> 00:59:40,995
How can we prove
that what he says is true?

854
00:59:41,078 --> 00:59:44,331
I won't force myself
on someone who doesn't love me back.

855
00:59:44,415 --> 00:59:45,958
I tried to stop it.

856
00:59:46,041 --> 00:59:48,002
I've never felt this way before.

857
00:59:48,085 --> 00:59:49,503
I want to prove my love for you.

858
00:59:50,254 --> 00:59:52,131
Diana, will you marry me?
